      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_6706ea7d1180d978cd39c9ab42dbf9ba71e08fbd5bbe6484a8cc31de2d7a09a5",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Hardy–Littlewood approximation reduces ζ(σ+it) to a Dirichlet polynomial, and partial summation reduces that control to short sums of n^{-it}=exp(-it log n) over ranges M≤N≤t. The earlier integral method is not efficiently available when N is much smaller than t, so the source explicitly proposes Taylor expansion to introduce polynomial structure into the logarithmic phase.",
