    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_14539fc8950e9d0d95cfb319ba35237d1d52b9730a88b2f72794532a25b16ede",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Taylor truncation fixes a degree r proportional to log t/log N, which in turn forces the usable Vinogradov moment order to be k=Cr². The residue-diversity/concentration induction supplies the scale-reduction engine behind that mean-value control, and the final assembly offsets its Hölder and moment losses by rational-denominator savings on a middle band of polynomial coefficients, yielding the exponential short-sum bound and its scale threshold.",
