    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_21da1ee0f8c42e81945e1f7f23e3c0a6d1df1e58344899a2152ae5ba607e3d0e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The short exponential-sum saving is transferred through three distinct interfaces: block decomposition and Abel summation insert the n^{-σ} weight to bound ζ near the one-line; Landau’s criterion turns the balanced growth bound into a wider zero-free region; and a contour shift with optimized height converts that region into the Vinogradov–Korobov prime-number-theorem remainder.",
